{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts | sed -n '1280,1365p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1280\t  }\n  1281\t\n  1282\t  /**\n  1283\t   * Enriches the durable `WorkingSetPlan` (just IDs) into the spec's\n  1284\t   * `HydrationPlan` (display names, version labels, accessMode) by reading\n  1285\t   * canonical artifact / source / output projections. The adapter receives the\n  1286\t   * richer projection so it can write meaningful filenames into the working\n  1287\t   * tree and decide what to clone.\n  1288\t   *\n  1289\t   * `fingerprint` is the persisted `workingSetFingerprint` from the durable\n  1290\t   * env-state row. The adapter sees the same digest the stale-projection path\n  1291\t   * uses, rather than a placeholder or a recomputed server-local hash.\n  1292\t   */\n  1293\t  private async buildAdapterHydrationPlan(args: {\n  1294\t    projectId: string;\n  1295\t    processId: string;\n  1296\t    plan: WorkingSetPlan;\n  1297\t  }): Promise<HydrationPlan> {\n  1298\t    const [artifacts, sources, outputs, fingerprint] = await Promise.all([\n  1299\t      this.platformStore.listProjectArtifacts({ projectId: args.projectId }),\n  1300\t      this.platformStore.listProjectSourceAttachments({ projectId: args.projectId }),\n  1301\t      this.platformStore.listProcessOutputs({ processId: args.processId }),\n  1302\t      this.platformStore.getProcessWorkingSetFingerprint({ processId: args.processId }),\n  1303\t    ]);\n  1304\t\n  1305\t    const artifactById = new Map(artifacts.map((artifact) => [artifact.artifactId, artifact]));\n  1306\t    const sourceById = new Map(sources.map((source) => [source.sourceAttachmentId, source]));\n  1307\t    const outputById = new Map(outputs.map((output) => [output.outputId, output]));\n  1308\t\n  1309\t    if (fingerprint === null) {\n  1310\t      throw new Error(\n  1311\t        `HydrationPlan is missing a persisted workingSetFingerprint for process '${args.processId}'.`,\n  1312\t      );\n  1313\t    }\n  1314\t\n  1315\t    return {\n  1316\t      fingerprint,\n  1317\t      artifactInputs: args.plan.artifactIds.map((artifactId) => {\n  1318\t        const artifact = artifactById.get(artifactId);\n  1319\t        return {\n  1320\t          artifactId,\n  1321\t          displayName: artifact?.displayName ?? artifactId,\n  1322\t          versionLabel: artifact?.currentVersionLabel ?? null,\n  1323\t        };\n  1324\t      }),\n  1325\t      outputInputs: args.plan.outputIds.map((outputId) => {\n  1326\t        const output = outputById.get(outputId);\n  1327\t        return {\n  1328\t          outputId,\n  1329\t          displayName: output?.displayName ?? outputId,\n  1330\t          revisionLabel: output?.revisionLabel ?? null,\n  1331\t        };\n  1332\t      }),\n  1333\t      sourceInputs: args.plan.sourceAttachmentIds.map((sourceAttachmentId) => {\n  1334\t        const source = sourceById.get(sourceAttachmentId);\n  1335\t        if (source === undefined) {\n  1336\t          // A plan referencing a source we can't resolve against the current\n  1337\t          // project-scoped sources is a real breakage — fail loud rather than\n  1338\t          // fabricating a placeholder repositoryUrl that would silently bypass\n  1339\t          // hydration or checkpointing.\n  1340\t          throw new Error(\n  1341\t            `HydrationPlan references sourceAttachmentId '${sourceAttachmentId}' that is not in the project's source listing.`,\n  1342\t          );\n  1343\t        }\n  1344\t        return {\n  1345\t          sourceAttachmentId,\n  1346\t          displayName: source.displayName,\n  1347\t          repositoryUrl: source.repositoryUrl,\n  1348\t          targetRef: source.targetRef,\n  1349\t          accessMode: source.accessMode,\n  1350\t        };\n  1351\t      }),\n  1352\t    };\n  1353\t  }\n  1354\t\n  1355\t  private async appendProcessEvent(args: {\n  1356\t    processId: string;\n  1357\t    text: string;\n  1358\t  }): Promise<ProcessHistoryItem> {\n  1359\t    return this.platformStore.appendProcessHistoryItem({\n  1360\t      processId: args.processId,\n  1361\t      kind: 'process_event',\n  1362\t      lifecycleState: 'finalized',\n  1363\t      text: args.text,\n  1364\t      relatedSideWorkId: null,\n  1365\t      relatedArtifactId: null,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md | sed -n '630,715p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md | sed -n '630,715p'\"","aggregated_output":"   630\t\n   631\tRead-only attachments can record `informed_work` but must not be represented as\n   632\t`received_code_update`. Code checkpoint planning already blocks writes to\n   633\tread-only sources; provenance records reinforce that boundary by deriving write\n   634\tprovenance only from successful writable checkpoint results.\n   635\t\n   636\tRefresh does not create provenance. Provenance is reserved for execution-time\n   637\tsource influence and durable code updates so AC-4 remains about process work,\n   638\tnot source maintenance.\n   639\t\n   640\t### Flow 5: Detach Sources\n   641\t\n   642\tThis flow covers AC-5.1 through AC-5.3. Detach is a soft operation. It removes\n   643\tthe source from future active source lists and current-source resolution, but it\n   644\tdoes not delete provenance or mutate an already hydrated working copy mid-run.\n   645\t\n   646\t```mermaid\n   647\tsequenceDiagram\n   648\t    participant U as User\n   649\t    participant C as Client Source UI\n   650\t    participant R as Fastify Source Route\n   651\t    participant S as SourceManagementService\n   652\t    participant P as PlatformStore\n   653\t    participant X as Convex\n   654\t\n   655\t    U->>C: Detach source\n   656\t    C->>R: DELETE source attachment\n   657\t    R->>S: detachSource\n   658\t    S->>P: softDetachSourceAttachment\n   659\t    P->>X: set detachedAt, detachedByUserId, updatedAt\n   660\t    X-->>P: detached row\n   661\t    P-->>S: detached response\n   662\t    S-->>R: detached true\n   663\t    R-->>C: remove from active list\n   664\t```\n   665\t\n   666\t### Flow 6: Reopen and Degraded State\n   667\t\n   668\tThis flow covers AC-6.1 through AC-6.3. Project shell and process work surface\n   669\treads continue to return section envelopes. One failed source/provenance lookup\n   670\tmust degrade locally rather than hiding healthy source rows.\n   671\t\n   672\t`SourceSectionReader` and `MaterialsSectionReader` should preserve the existing\n   673\tsection envelope pattern. Active lists exclude detached rows; process materials\n   674\tuse the active-source resolver to combine project and process scopes. If an\n   675\tenrichment lookup fails, the reader returns durable source identity with\n   676\t`entryStatus: degraded` or a section-level source error only when the whole\n   677\tsection cannot load.\n   678\t\n   679\t## Active Source Resolution\n   680\t\n   681\tThe active-source resolver is the central design answer for process-scoped\n   682\tshadowing. It affects the process work surface and environment working-set\n   683\tplanning; it does not make every project-scoped source automatically current\n   684\tfor every process. A process sees only source attachments referenced by its\n   685\tcurrent material refs, after active filtering and shadowing are applied.\n   686\t\n   687\t```typescript\n   688\texport function resolveActiveProcessSources(args: {\n   689\t  projectSources: SourceAttachmentSummary[];\n   690\t  processId: string;\n   691\t  currentSourceAttachmentIds: string[];\n   692\t}): ProcessSourceReference[] {\n   693\t  throw new NotImplementedError('resolveActiveProcessSources');\n   694\t}\n   695\t```\n   696\t\n   697\tResolution rules:\n   698\t\n   699\t1. Exclude rows with `detachedAt`.\n   700\t2. Build the base active set from rows whose `sourceAttachmentId` is in\n   701\t   `currentSourceAttachmentIds`.\n   702\t3. Partition active rows into project-scoped rows and rows where `processId`\n   703\t   matches.\n   704\t4. Compute shadow key as `${repositoryFullName}:${targetRef ?? ''}`.\n   705\t5. If an active project-scoped row has a process-scoped sibling with the same\n   706\t   shadow key, include the process-scoped sibling in the candidate set even when\n   707\t   its id is not yet in `currentSourceAttachmentIds`.\n   708\t6. Prefer the matching process-scoped row over the project-scoped row for that\n   709\t   process only.\n   710\t7. Sort visible rows by `updatedAt` descending.\n   711\t8. Preserve degraded metadata independently per row.\n   712\t\n   713\tThis resolver belongs in Fastify/shared server logic, not Convex. Convex stores\n   714\trows; Fastify decides how one process sees its current source material.\n   715\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
